.TH GO-DHCPD-CONFIG.JSON5 5 "October 2026" "go-dhcpd 1.8.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
go-dhcpd-config.json5 \- configuration file format for the go-dhcpd daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/go-dhcpd/config.json5
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B config.json5
is the JSON5 configuration file read by
.BR dhcpd (8)
at startup (see
.BR \-\-config
in
.BR dhcpd (8)
to use a path other than the default). It is a single JSON object with
five top-level members:
.BR global ", " auth ", " plugins ", " subnets ", and " static .
.PP
The
.B subnets
and
.B static
arrays are only meaningful when the active config-provider plugin is
.BR go\-dhcpd\-file\-config (3),
which reads them directly from this file. When
.BR go\-dhcpd\-sqlite3\-config (3)
is the active plugin, subnet and static-host data instead lives in its
SQLite3 database, and the
.B subnets
/
.B static
arrays in this file are ignored (see
.BR go\-dhcpd\-migration\-tool (8)
for moving existing data between the two).
.SH FILE FORMAT
.B config.json5
is parsed as JSON5, a superset of JSON that is more forgiving to hand-edit:
.TP
.B \(bu
.B //
line comments and
.B /* */
block comments are permitted anywhere.
.TP
.B \(bu
Trailing commas are permitted in objects and arrays.
.TP
.B \(bu
Object keys may be unquoted identifiers, though this file consistently
uses quoted string keys for clarity.
.TP
.B \(bu
Single-quoted strings are accepted in addition to double-quoted strings.
.PP
.B Caveat:
an object whose body contains only comments and no actual member, e.g.
.RS
.nf
"settings": { // nothing configured yet
}
.fi
.RE
fails to parse. Use a truly empty object instead, \fI"settings": {}\fP,
and keep any explanatory comment outside the braces.
.SH GLOBAL
The
.B global
object controls server-wide behavior and is required.
.TP
.BR lease_time " (integer, seconds, default " 86400 )
Default DHCP lease duration offered to clients.
.TP
.BR netbios_node_type " (integer, default " 8 )
Default NetBIOS node type advertised to clients (option 46) unless
overridden per-subnet.
.RB "Valid values: " 1 " (B-node), " 2 " (P-node), " 4 " (M-node), " 8
(H-node, recommended).
.TP
.BR ping_timeout " (integer, milliseconds, default " 1000 )
How long the allocator waits for an ICMP echo reply when checking that a
candidate address is unused before offering it.
.TP
.BR ping_retries " (integer, default " 2 )
Number of ping attempts made against a candidate address before it is
considered free.
.TP
.BR database_path " (string, default " /var/lib/go-dhcpd/dhcpd.db )
Path to the daemon's lease-tracking SQLite3 database (distinct from any
database used by the
.B sqlite3-config
plugin).
.TP
.BR listen_address " (string, default " 0.0.0.0 )
IP address the UDP port-67 listener binds to, for unicast and
relay-agent traffic.
.B Deprecated:
prefer
.B listen_interface
to restrict both the UDP and raw-socket listeners to one NIC.
.TP
.BR listen_interface " (string, default empty \(em all interfaces)"
Network interface name (e.g.
.IR eth0 ", " ens33 )
that both the raw AF_PACKET listener and the UDP port-67 listener are
restricted to. Leave empty to listen on all interfaces.
.TP
.BR api_port " (integer, default " 18467 )
TCP port the REST API listens on.
.TP
.B tls
(object) Controls whether the REST API is served over HTTPS instead of
plain HTTP. See
.B TLS
below.
.SS TLS
Nested under
.BR global.tls .
.TP
.BR enabled " (boolean, default " false )
Serve the REST API over HTTPS. Strongly recommended whenever the API is
reachable over anything but a fully trusted loopback/local link, since
HTTP Basic Auth credentials are otherwise sent in the clear.
.TP
.B cert_file
Path to a PEM-encoded certificate (chain), readable by the daemon.
Required when
.B enabled
is true.
.TP
.B key_file
Path to the matching PEM-encoded private key, readable by the daemon.
Required when
.B enabled
is true.
.PP
The daemon enforces a minimum of TLS 1.2.
.SH AUTH
The
.B auth
object controls which non-root accounts may reach authenticated REST API
endpoints. Credentials are verified via PAM (service
.IR go\-dhcpd ,
see
.BR pam.d/ (5)
files in the go-dhcpd source distribution);
.B root
is always authorized regardless of these lists.
.TP
.BR allowed_users " ([]string, default " [] )
Local account names permitted to authenticate.
.TP
.BR allowed_groups " ([]string, default " [] )
Local group names whose members are permitted to authenticate.
.PP
If both lists are empty, only
.B root
can reach authenticated endpoints.
.SH PLUGINS
The
.B plugins
object configures the daemon's config-provider plugin, under
.BR plugins.config_provider .
.TP
.BR name " (string, default " file\-config )
Plugin identifier, also used to derive the default
.B path
below.
.TP
.BR path " (string, optional)"
Path to the plugin executable. When omitted, defaults to
.IR \fI<plugin_dir>\fP/\fI<name>\fP.plugin ,
where
.I <plugin_dir>
is the plugin directory baked into the
.B dhcpd
binary at build time (see
.BR dhcpd (8)).
.TP
.BR settings " (object, default " {} )
Plugin-specific settings, passed to the plugin on every invocation. The
bundled
.B file-config
plugin reads
.BR config_path " (string), which defaults to this configuration file's"
own path when not set. The bundled
.B sqlite3-config
plugin requires
.BR db_path " (string), the path to its SQLite3 database file."
.SH SUBNETS
.B subnets
is an array of objects, each describing one IPv4 subnet served by the
daemon. Only read when
.B file-config
is the active config-provider plugin.
.TP
.BR network " (string, required)"
Subnet's network address, e.g.
.IR 192.168.1.0 .
.TP
.BR netmask " (string, required)"
Subnet mask, e.g.
.IR 255.255.255.0 .
.TP
.BR dynamic_ranges " ([]object, default " [] )
Dynamic allocation pools. Each entry has
.BR start_address " and " end_address
(strings, both inclusive IPv4 addresses).
.TP
.BR enable_bootp " (boolean, default " false )
Serves RFC 951 BOOTREQUESTs on this subnet. When enabled, only clients
with a matching entry in
.B static
are answered; any other client's BOOTREQUEST is silently ignored, since
BootP has no dynamic-allocation concept. See
.BR next_server ", " server_hostname ", and " boot_filename
below to supply boot-server information in the reply.
.TP
.BR next_server " (string, optional)"
BootP
.IR siaddr :
the IPv4 address of the boot/TFTP server to use, if different from this
daemon. Left as
.I 0.0.0.0
in replies when unset.
.TP
.BR server_hostname " (string, optional, max 63 bytes)"
BootP
.IR sname :
the boot server's hostname, included verbatim in replies when set.
.TP
.BR boot_filename " (string, optional, max 127 bytes)"
BootP
.IR file :
the path to the boot file the client should fetch, included verbatim in
replies when set.
.TP
.BR netbios_node_type " (integer, optional)"
Per-subnet override of
.BR global.netbios_node_type .
.TP
.BR domain_name_servers " ([]string, default " [] )
DNS servers offered to clients (option 6).
.TP
.BR domain_name " (string, optional)"
Domain name offered to clients (option 15).
.TP
.BR domain_search " ([]string, default " [] )
DNS search list offered to clients (option 119).
.TP
.BR interface_mtu " (integer, optional)"
Interface MTU offered to clients (option 26).
.TP
.BR ntp_servers " ([]string, default " [] )
NTP servers offered to clients (option 42).
.TP
.BR time_servers " ([]string, default " [] )
Time protocol (RFC 868) servers offered to clients (option 4).
.TP
.BR smtp_servers " ([]string, default " [] )
SMTP servers offered to clients (option 69).
.TP
.BR lpr_servers " ([]string, default " [] )
LPR servers offered to clients (option 9).
.TP
.BR netbios_name_servers " ([]string, default " [] )
NetBIOS name (WINS) servers offered to clients (option 44).
.TP
.BR netbios_dd_servers " ([]string, default " [] )
NetBIOS datagram distribution servers offered to clients (option 45).
.TP
.BR routers " ([]string, default " [] )
Default gateway(s) offered to clients (option 3).
.PP
All IPv4-valued fields above (
.BR network ", " netmask ", dynamic range addresses, and every " []string
server-list field) must be valid IPv4 literals; IPv6 is not supported.
.SH STATIC
.B static
is an array of objects, each a static (reserved) DHCP assignment. Only
read when
.B file-config
is the active config-provider plugin.
.TP
.BR mac_address " (string, required)"
Client hardware address, in
.I aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff
format. Must be a 6-byte Ethernet address; matching is case-insensitive.
.TP
.BR ip_address " (string, required)"
Address to assign to this client. May be an IPv4 literal or a hostname
resolved via DNS at allocation time.
.TP
.BR hostname " (string, optional)"
Hostname stored as static-lease metadata; not currently sent to the client as option 12.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.RS
{
  "global": {
    "lease_time": 86400,
    "database_path": "/var/lib/go-dhcpd/dhcpd.db",
    "listen_interface": "eth0",
    "api_port": 18467
  },
  "auth": {
    "allowed_users": ["admin"],
    "allowed_groups": ["go-dhcpd-admins"]
  },
  "plugins": {
    "config_provider": { "name": "file-config", "settings": {} }
  },
  "subnets": [
    {
      "network": "192.168.1.0",
      "netmask": "255.255.255.0",
      "dynamic_ranges": [
        { "start_address": "192.168.1.100", "end_address": "192.168.1.163" }
      ],
      "domain_name_servers": ["192.168.1.1"],
      "routers": ["192.168.1.1"]
    }
  ],
  "static": [
    { "mac_address": "aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff", "ip_address": "192.168.1.10",
      "hostname": "server1.example.local" }
  ]
}
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/go-dhcpd/config.json5
Default location read by
.BR dhcpd (8).
.TP
.I /etc/go-dhcpd/config.json5.example
Fully annotated example, installed by
.BR "make install" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dhcpd (8),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-migration\-tool (8),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-file\-config (3),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-sqlite3\-config (3)
